---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { operator } from '../legal';

const sections = [
  { id: 'who-we-are', title: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'on-your-device', title: 'What stays on your device' },
  { id: 'open-library', title: 'Open Library and covers' },
  { id: 'goodreads', title: 'Goodreads CSV imports' },
  { id: 'permissions', title: 'Device features and permissions' },
  { id: 'scanner', title: 'Android scanner diagnostics' },
  { id: 'exports', title: 'Exports and external services' },
  { id: 'website', title: 'This website and contact' },
  { id: 'retention', title: 'Storage, retention, and deletion' },
  { id: 'legal-bases', title: 'Legal bases and international data' },
  { id: 'your-rights', title: 'Your choices and rights' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes to this policy' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How Wovenleaf handles your local library, Goodreads imports, Open Library searches, device permissions, scanner diagnostics, and website visits."
  summary="Your library lives on your device. Here is what stays there, when an online service is involved, and the choices you have."
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="who-we-are">
    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Wovenleaf is provided by {operator.name}, based in {operator.country}. We
      are responsible for the personal information we process in operating
      Wovenleaf and this website. You can contact us at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${operator.email}`}>{operator.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      This policy covers the mobile app and its landing website. The app has no
      Wovenleaf account, cloud library, advertising, or social profile. We do
      not receive a copy of your library or sell your personal information.
      Online book services, Android scanner diagnostics, and website hosting are
      explained separately below.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="on-your-device">
    <h2>2. What stays on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Wovenleaf stores and processes your library in its local database and app
      storage. Depending on the features you use, this includes:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Books, identifiers, covers, shelves, lists, ratings, and private notes.
      </li>
      <li>
        Reading and listening history, progress, bookmarks, highlights, and
        preferences.
      </li>
      <li>
        Imported CSV records, import history, EPUBs, audiobooks, and associated
        files.
      </li>
      <li>
        Voice notes you record, search history or cached results, and local
        recovery copies.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Reading, listening, organization, file inspection, and local library
      search take place on your device. Searching private notes, if enabled, is
      also local. Wovenleaf does not upload your EPUBs, audiobooks, recordings,
      notes, or full CSV export to us or to a book-search provider.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="open-library">
    <h2>3. Open Library and covers</h2>
    <p>
      Online catalog search and metadata enrichment contact <a
        href="https://openlibrary.org/">Open Library</a
      >, operated by the Internet Archive. Requests may contain your search
      text, a book’s ISBN, title or author, and your language preference. The
      provider also receives the IP address and technical request information
      needed to handle the connection. These requests can reveal which books you
      are interested in.
    </p>
    <p>
      Displaying a remotely hosted cover can contact Open Library’s cover
      servers or the image host returned in its book data. The host receives the
      requested image address and connection information, even when you are
      viewing an existing library entry rather than making a new search.
      Wovenleaf caches some search results locally to reduce repeated lookups.
    </p>
    <p>
      These services have their own logging and retention practices. See the{
        ' '
      }
      <a href="https://archive.org/about/terms"
        >Internet Archive’s privacy policy and terms</a
      >. Your private notes, ratings, reading progress, and book file contents
      are not included in Wovenleaf’s metadata requests.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="goodreads">
    <h2>4. Goodreads CSV imports</h2>
    <p>
      You obtain your export from Goodreads and choose or share the CSV file
      with Wovenleaf. The app parses it, prepares the review, matches records,
      and applies the import locally. It does not receive your Goodreads login
      credentials, sign in for you, or send changes back to Goodreads.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong
        >After import, missing covers may be filled in automatically through
        Open Library.</strong
      > This sends ISBNs and, where needed, a title and author from the imported records,
      along with your language preference. Lookups can retry when you reopen or return
      to the app. The CSV file itself and its private review, rating, or shelf data
      are not uploaded. Opening the Goodreads export page takes you to their website
      under their own policies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="permissions">
    <h2>5. Device features and permissions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Camera:</strong> used when you choose to scan an ISBN. Barcode recognition
        runs on the device; a resulting ISBN may be used for an online book lookup.
        Android scanner diagnostics are described below.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Microphone:</strong> used when you start a private voice note. Playback
        pauses before recording. The recording is saved locally.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Files and images:</strong> Wovenleaf reads the documents, audiobook
        files, or cover images you select or share with it. A file provider you choose
        may first download a file from your own cloud storage.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Clipboard and sharing:</strong> the app can read an ISBN when you
        use its paste action, or receive text and files you share with it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Audio and notifications:</strong> system media controls support background
        listening. If you enable “Show book details when locked”, titles, authors,
        chapters, and covers can appear on the lock screen and connected system media
        surfaces.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can change permissions in your device settings. Declining a permission
      may disable the feature that needs it; you can still enter books manually
      and use other available features.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="scanner">
    <h2>6. Android scanner diagnostics</h2>
    <p>
      The Android ISBN scanner uses Google ML Kit. Although image recognition
      happens on the device, Google’s SDK collects diagnostic and usage data,
      including device model and operating system, app version, installation
      identifiers, performance, configuration, and feature or error events.
      Google receives this data over HTTPS for diagnostics and usage analytics.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is a third-party exception to local processing, not a Wovenleaf
      reading-activity analytics service. See <a
        href="https://developers.google.com/ml-kit/android-data-disclosure"
        >Google’s ML Kit data disclosure</a
      >{' '}
      and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
        >Google’s privacy policy</a
      >. You can type or paste an ISBN instead of using the camera scanner.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="exports">
    <h2>7. Exports and external services</h2>
    <p>
      Exports and backups are created on your device. Depending on the format
      and options, they can include library records, ratings, notes,
      annotations, and EPUB files. Wovenleaf does not encrypt exported files.
      Review the contents before saving or sharing them: your chosen recipient
      or storage provider will have access, and a cloud-synced folder may upload
      them.
    </p>
    <p>
      EPUBs can contain web links or references to online resources. Opening an
      external link or loading a remote resource can contact its host, which
      receives connection information and the requested address. That host’s
      privacy practices apply. App-store links and other websites you choose to
      open likewise take you outside Wovenleaf.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your operating system, app store, email service, and selected document or
      sharing providers may process information under their own settings and
      policies. Wovenleaf has no automatic library upload or cloud-sync service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="website">
    <h2>8. This website and contact</h2>
    <p>
      This landing website is hosted by Vercel. Delivering pages and protecting
      the site involves processing connection and request information, such as
      IP address, browser or device information, requested page, timestamp, and
      referrer when supplied. This is separate from your app library, which is
      not sent to the website.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not add advertising cookies, tracking pixels, or visitor analytics
      scripts to this website. Fonts and images are served with the site.
      Hosting and security processing are described in <a
        href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-notice"
        >Vercel’s privacy notice</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you email us, we receive your address, message, and any attachments you
      choose to send. We use them to respond, investigate your request, and
      maintain necessary support or legal records. Do not send your library or
      private files unless they are needed for your request. Our email provider
      processes that correspondence to deliver and store it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="retention">
    <h2>9. Storage, retention, and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Local records remain in app storage until you remove them or clear the
      app’s data. Import history, cached data, and recovery copies may retain
      earlier versions after an entry is edited or removed. To remove all
      Wovenleaf-managed data on a device, use the operating system’s option to
      clear app data or delete the app and its data; merely offloading an app
      may preserve data. Delete any separately saved exports and original source
      files from their own locations if you no longer want them.
    </p>
    <p>
      The app configures its private storage to be excluded from automatic
      platform backups. Local recovery points remain on the device. Device
      behavior and copies you save elsewhere are controlled by the relevant
      platform or provider. We cannot recover or remotely erase data we do not
      possess.
    </p>
    <p>
      Protection relies on your device’s security and app sandbox; the library
      database and exports do not have additional Wovenleaf encryption. Use a
      device lock and protect your backups.
    </p>
    <p>
      We keep correspondence only as long as needed to handle the request,
      follow up, and meet applicable recordkeeping or legal-claim obligations.
      Hosting logs and third-party diagnostics follow their providers’ retention
      practices, which depend on operational, security, and legal needs. We do
      not maintain a separate server-side history of your reading or catalog
      searches.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="legal-bases">
    <h2>10. Legal bases and international data</h2>
    <p>
      Where European data protection law applies, processing necessary to
      provide the app features you request is based on performing our agreement
      with you. We rely on legitimate interests to deliver and secure this
      website, respond to general inquiries, and maintain the reliability of
      optional scanner functionality. Where a legal obligation applies, that
      obligation is the basis for the relevant processing. If processing
      requires consent, we must obtain it separately; this policy is not a
      request for blanket consent.
    </p>
    <p>
      Local-only records are not transferred to us. Online requests and
      correspondence may be processed outside your country, including in the
      United States, by the Internet Archive, Google, Vercel, or the services
      you choose. Those providers explain their processing and transfer
      safeguards in their policies. For transfers we are responsible for, we use
      safeguards required by applicable law, such as an adequacy decision or
      standard contractual clauses where applicable. Contact us for information
      about safeguards relevant to your request.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="your-rights">
    <h2>11. Your choices and rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can view and edit your library in the app, export it from Settings →
      Advanced, manage permissions in your device settings, and remove local
      data as described above. Using the app without network access prevents
      online searches, automatic cover lookups, and other outbound requests
      while offline; already available local content remains usable.
    </p>
    <p>
      Depending on your location and the processing involved, you may have
      rights to access, correct, delete, or obtain a portable copy of personal
      information, restrict processing, object to processing based on legitimate
      interests, or withdraw consent without affecting earlier lawful
      processing. We do not use your information for automated decisions with
      legal or similarly significant effects.
    </p>
    <p>
      Send requests to <a href={`mailto:${operator.email}`}>{operator.email}</a
      >. We will respond within the period required by law, generally one month
      for GDPR requests, and explain any lawful extension. We may need limited
      information to verify a request. We cannot retrieve a local library we do
      not hold. You may also complain to your local data protection authority,
      including the <a href="https://www.aepd.es/"
        >Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD)</a
      >{' '}
      where applicable.
    </p>
    <p>
      Wovenleaf is a general-purpose reading app and is not directed
      specifically at children. We do not request a child’s age or create child
      profiles. A parent or guardian who believes a child has sent us personal
      information can contact us to request its removal, subject to applicable
      law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      Our intention is to keep your reading library local to your device. We
      will update this policy when the app, website, or relevant data practices
      change and show the new date here. Material changes will receive any
      notice or consent required by law before the new processing begins. See
      also the <a href="/terms/">terms of service</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
